Author: vincent <vincent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 26 07:03:23 2026 +1000

    agent: a comment between dsh patch-list entries survives a rewrite (#3329)
    
    dshParse gave the lines before the first entry to head (#2667) and a flow
    list's tail to its entry (#2674), but a comment line at the left edge between
    two entries fell into the default branch: it was appended to the entry before
    it. dshPutRoute and dshPutSearch rebuild an entry's lines whole — yaml.Node
    carries no comments, and dshSearchLines is a template — so the next round
    dropped the comment. Vibe Island's managed block lost its begin marker within
    30 seconds while its closing marker, attached to the entry magpie does not
    rebuild, stayed: the tool then refused to edit the file ("closing marker
    without a begin marker").
    
    A comment or blank line at the left edge between entries is now kept as its
    own entry between the two, so no rebuild of either can take it. An indented
    line still belongs to the entry before it, so what a genuine patch entry is
    does not change.
    
    Not the following entry instead: a marker does precede the block it guards,
    but that entry may itself be one magpie writes again (agent-default-model,
    llm-pi-ai, web-search-deepseek), and the comment would be lost in that turn
    rather than this one. Kept between them, it survives whichever is rewritten.
    
    RED->GREEN: TestDshCommentsBetweenEntriesSurviveRewrite (internal/agent)
    writes the reporter's file — magpie's route, Vibe Island's
    ">>> vibe-island managed block >>>" comment, its - insert: entry and the
    "<<< ... <<<" comment — then takes one keepDshWired round (dshRouteAgain) with
    the catalog's route. At 01468003 it failed: "the managed block's comment
    markers lost". With this change it passes, and the block is written back whole.
    
    Ran: go test -tags nogui ./internal/agent (ok), gofmt -l on the changed files
    (empty), go vet ./..., GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go vet -tags nogui ./...,
    GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./..., go build ./... and the linux nogui and
    windows builds — all ok. Not tried: dsh itself reading the written profile on
    macOS.

diff --git a/internal/agent/dsh.go b/internal/agent/dsh.go
index b81e5e63..0598acec 100644
--- a/internal/agent/dsh.go
+++ b/internal/agent/dsh.go
@@ -469,6 +469,13 @@ func dshParse(path, raw string) (head []string, items []dshItem, err error) {
 		case t != "" && !strings.HasPrefix(t, "#") && !strings.HasPrefix(l, " "):
 			return nil, nil, fmt.Errorf("%s is not a list of entries magpie can edit", path)
 		default:
+			// a comment or a blank line between entries is kept as its own, not
+			// as the previous entry's last lines: an entry magpie writes again
+			// replaces its lines whole, and the comment went with them (#3329)
+			if !strings.HasPrefix(l, " ") {
+				items = append(items, dshItem{lines: []string{l}})
+				continue
+			}
 			items[len(items)-1].lines = append(items[len(items)-1].lines, l)
 		}
 		it := &items[len(items)-1]
